- In python/sglang/srt/function_call/gpt_oss_detector.py, update parse_streaming_increment:
- If a streaming chunk produces no Harmony events and the buffer contains no Harmony structural markers (<|start|>, <|channel|>, <|message|>, <|constrain|>, <|end|>, <|call|>, <|
return|>, assistantfinal), treat the buffered text as plain content and emit it immediately as normal_text, then clear the buffer.
- This preserves streaming of non-tool content even when tools are provided but not used.
- Tool calls remain governed by Harmony events when markers are present; reasoning streaming is unchanged.

