## Motivation

During gRPC streaming, when the final output arrives, the server was sending only a `GenerateComplete` response and skipping the `GenerateChunk`. This means gRPC clients that consume tokens exclusively from chunk messages would miss the last batch of tokens.

The fix ensures the server always yields a chunk response first, then follows with the completion response when finished. The client reads tokens from chunks and treats the completion as a "done" signal with metadata (finish_reason, token counts, etc.).

## Modifications

- Changed the streaming branch in `Generate` handler (`grpc_server.py`) to always emit a chunk, then conditionally emit a completion if finished — instead of the previous exclusive either/or logic.

## Accuracy Tests

Tested with `Llama-4-Maverick-17B-128E-Instruct-FP8` streaming + stop words.

Before this fix, the last chunk was not emitted during streaming — only a `GenerateComplete` was sent. gRPC clients that consume tokens from chunks only would miss the last batch of tokens. After this fix, the last chunk is always sent before the completion.

For example, with `no_stop_trim=true` and `stop=["5"]`, the token `"5"` now correctly appears in the last chunk before the completion signal. Before this fix, the chunk containing `"5"` was skipped entirely.

